---
/* Questions a reader has and two honest notes, the Rin site's closing shape. */
const qs = [
  ['Are the demos real?', 'They are the real products rebuilt in HTML so they can run inside this page. volbase’s window shows captures of the live site. Rin’s terminal and Kyou’s quick-add answer what you type. Market Station’s tiles random-walk from real readings. There is no stock screenshot anywhere on this page.'],
  ['Can I use any of them?', 'volbase is live at volbase.app. Rin is free and open source, with the code on GitHub. Kyou is still being built. Market Station runs for one reader at home and isn’t public.'],
  ['What did you build them with?', 'Swift and SwiftUI for Rin and Kyou, with AppKit where SwiftUI wouldn’t reach. Next.js, Supabase, and Stripe for volbase. Python and FastAPI for Market Station. Claude Code sits in the loop for all four, and Rin is built around it.'],
  ['Who is this site for?', 'Anyone who googled the name and would rather see the work than read about it.'],
];
---
<section class="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="faq-head head up">
    <p class="eyebrow">Before you ask</p>
    <h2 id="faq-title">Questions you probably have</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="qs">
    {qs.map(([q, a]) => (
      <details class="q up"><summary>{q}</summary><p>{a}</p></details>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="notes" aria-label="Two honest notes">
  <div class="note up">
    <h3>Kyou isn’t out yet</h3>
    <p>The demo runs the real screens, but the app is still being built and hasn’t shipped.
      When it does, the link goes here.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="note up">
    <h3>No number here is invented</h3>
    <p>Every figure on this page comes from the record: the products, the placements, the
      dates. Where there wasn’t a number, there isn’t one on the page.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq { padding-top: var(--sec); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.5fr; gap: 24px 64px; align-items: start; max-width: var(--wrap); margin-inline: auto; padding-inline: var(--gut); }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .faq { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 34px; } }
  .faq-head { position: sticky; top: 104px; }
  .faq-head h2 { max-width: 13ch; }
  .q { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .q:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .q summary { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 16px; cursor: pointer; padding: 20px 0; font-size: var(--t-body); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.015em; list-style: none; color: var(--ink); }
  .q summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .q summary::after {
    content: ""; flex: none; margin-left: auto; margin-top: 8px; width: 12px; height: 12px;
    background: linear-gradient(var(--ink-3) 0 0) center / 100% 1.8px no-repeat, linear-gradient(var(--ink-3) 0 0) center / 1.8px 100% no-repeat;
    transition: transform .4s var(--boing), background-size .3s var(--settle);
  }
  .q[open] summary::after { transform: rotate(180deg); background-size: 100% 1.8px, 1.8px 0; }
  .q p { padding: 0 40px 24px 0; font-size: var(--t-ui); color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 54ch; }

  .notes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; padding-top: var(--sec); max-width: var(--wrap); margin-inline: auto; padding-inline: var(--gut); }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .notes { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .note { border: 1px dashed color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink-3) 55%, transparent); border-radius: var(--r-card); padding: 24px 26px; }
  .note h3 { font-size: var(--t-copy); font-weight: 800; }
  .note p { margin-top: 9px; font-size: var(--t-small); color: var(--ink-2); line-height: 1.6; }
</style>
